[gd_resource type="Theme" load_steps=12 format=3]

; The whole game's look, in one place.
;
; Set as the project's default theme (Project Settings -> GUI -> Theme ->
; Custom), so every Control in every scene picks it up without being told:
; the combat HUD, the pause menu, the reaction prompt, the result screen. That
; is the point of it being a Theme rather than more inline colours - before
; this, each panel set its own, which is why none of them matched.
;
; The palette is the one the battle selector already uses. Those seven colours
; are named as constants at the top of ui/level_select.gd; if you re-tint,
; change both.
;
;   dce8f5  headings
;   c2ceda  body text
;   8296a9  labels, counts, anything secondary
;   4a86c8  accent: focus, hover, the edge of the thing you are on
;   19212c  panels
;   1c2531  a card at rest
;   24344a  a card under the cursor
;   2b3947  borders
;   2b3542  the empty part of a bar

